```java
public class PowerOfThree {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        return (n > 0) && (n % 3 == 1) && ((n - 1) % powOfThree(3) == 0);
    }

    private long powOfThree(long base) {
        long result = 1;
        while ((result * base) <= Integer.MAX_VALUE) {
            result *= base;
        }
        return result;
    }
}
```

This solution uses a recursive helper function `powOfThree` to calculate the maximum possible value of `3^n` for a given `n`. If `n` is positive and its remainder when divided by 3 is 1, it means that `n` can be expressed as `3^k * 4`, where `3^k` is a power of three. The last check ensures that `k * log(3) * log(n) == log(n)`, where `log(n)` is the largest power of three that divides `n`.

